# Third-party notices

## DeepSeek Harness (DSH) — MIT

The English source strings this package translates, and the key names it
targets, come from the DSH web client packages published by DeepSeek:

- `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-*` (MIT), and the DSH application bundle that ships them
- Upstream repository: <https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness>
- Copyright (c) DeepSeek

`reference/en/*.json` is a snapshot of those packages' `en` dictionaries,
extracted from an installed DSH `0.2.0-rc.2` with `tools/extract-dicts.py`. It is
committed only so that contributors can diff translations and run
`tools/verify.mjs` without a DSH installation. No DSH source code is copied; only
the locale key names and their English values, which this package must match.

## Noto Sans JP — SIL Open Font License 1.1

This package does **not** redistribute the Noto Sans JP font. `locale/ja/font.css`
only names it in a `font-family` stack, so the font is used if the reader has
installed it (for example `brew install --cask font-noto-sans-jp`, or from
<https://fonts.google.com/noto/specimen/Noto+Sans+JP>). Without it, the stack
falls back to the Japanese system fonts already present (Hiragino Sans on macOS,
Yu Gothic UI / Meiryo on Windows).

